:: Introduction [intro-bg] {"position": "700,200", "size": "100,100"}
{<div class="scene">
<div class="scene-title">The Last Train Home<span class="scene-sub">MIDNIGHT EXPRESS — LINE 0</span></div>
<div class="ticket-name"><span class="ticket-ink">Traveler</span></div>
</div>}
<div class="name-field"><span class="name-label">Write your name on the ticket</span>(input-box: bind $name, "X", 1, "Traveler")</div>

The platform is silent, shrouded in thick yellow fog. The metallic groan of iron wheels cutting through the night breaks the quiet.

Before boarding, you glance down at the ticket in your hand.

{<div class="choices">[[Board the Train->Carriage 1 Choices]]</div>}


:: Carriage 1 Choices {"position": "900,300", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 1)(if: (trimmed: $name) is "")[(set: $name to "Traveler")](else:)[(set: $name to (trimmed: $name))]

The heavy iron door slides shut behind you with an ominous latch. The train rattles forward, lurching into motion.

The passenger car is dimly lit, the velvet seats worn thin. An old conductor in a faded uniform approaches, his eyes sunken and gray.

“Ticket, please,” he rasps, scanning your ticket. “Ah, $name. You barely made the last run.”

(if: $sanity >= 80)[
“Make sure you stay in your seat until the final stop,” he adds softly.
](else:)[
“You don’t look so good, $name...” he whispers.
]

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Ask the conductor where this train is headed")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 3))(go-to: "Talk to Conductor")]
(link: "Ignore him and explore the forward car")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 5))(set: $trustsConductor to false)(go-to: "Explore Carriage")]
(link: "Follow his instructions and take a seat")[(go-to: "Take a Seat")]
</div>}


:: Talk to Conductor {"position": "700,500", "size": "100,100"}
(unless: $clues contains "warning")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "warning"))]The conductor stops.

“Home, of course.”

“And where exactly is that?”

He looks down at your ticket, then back at you.

“That depends on the passenger.”

Before you can respond, he slips the ticket punch into his coat pocket.

“One piece of advice. If you hear someone calling your name from outside the train, do not answer.”

He turns and disappears through the forward door.


{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->The Announcement]]</div>}


:: Explore Carriage {"position": "900,500", "size": "100,100"}
You brush past the conductor and continue down the aisle.

The seats are empty, yet several appear recently occupied. A newspaper lies open on one, and a half-finished cup of coffee rests on another.

Strangely, the coffee is still warm.

You pick up the newspaper.

The date reads October 28, 1891.

<span class="examine">(link: "Read the headline")[(unless: $clues contains "newspaper")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "newspaper"))](rerun: ?data)<span class="examined"><span class="sign">MIDNIGHT EXPRESS LOST IN FOG</span><br>//Line Zero departed Ashgrove at midnight and never arrived. Among the missing: the conductor, eleven passengers, and a boy, nine years old, travelling alone.//</span>]</span>

Behind you, the conductor clears his throat.

“Curiosity is a dangerous habit aboard this train.”

You turn around.

But he’s already gone.

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->The Announcement]]</div>}


:: Take a Seat {"position": "1100,500", "size": "100,100"}
(unless: $clues contains "armrest")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "armrest"))]You settle into one of the worn velvet seats.

The train rocks gently beneath you. Outside, the fog has grown so thick that even the station lights have disappeared.

You glance at the seat across from yours.

Someone has scratched a message into the wooden armrest.

“DON’T FALL ASLEEP.”

<span class="examine">(link: "Run your thumb over the scratches")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 2))(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">The grooves are fresh. Splinters still curl at the edges. The letters lean the way yours do when you write in a hurry.</span>]</span>

You look toward the conductor.

He’s standing at the far end of the carriage.

Watching you.

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->The Announcement]]</div>}


:: The Announcement [flicker] {"position": "900,700", "size": "100,100"}
The carriage lights flicker.

Once.

Twice.

A low electrical hum fills the air. Somewhere beneath your feet, the wheels begin to screech against the tracks.

Then, without warning, the overhead speakers crackle to life.

<div class="speaker">“Good evening, passengers. Welcome aboard the Midnight Express, Line Zero.”</div>
The voice is feminine, almost comforting.

<div class="speaker">“For your safety, please keep your belongings close and remain inside the train at all times.”</div>
A short burst of static interrupts the announcement.

<div class="speaker">“Our next scheduled stop is…”</div>
Silence.

<div class="speaker">“We apologize. That station no longer exists.”</div>
The speaker clicks off.

You stare at the ceiling, waiting for an explanation that never comes.

Suddenly, a sharp metallic sound echoes from the far end of the carriage.

The door connecting to the next car has opened.

Beyond it, you hear something you haven’t heard since boarding.

Another passenger.

A woman is crying.

What do you do?

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Investigate the crying")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 0))(go-to: "Carriage 2")]
(link: "Search the carriage before leaving")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 3))(unless: $clues contains "conductor-notebook")[(set: $clues to $clues + (a: "conductor-notebook"))](go-to: "Search the Carriage")]
(link: "Attempt to return to the platform")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 5))(go-to: "Return to the Platform")]
</div>}


:: Search the Carriage {"position": "550,1700", "size": "100,100"}
The crying continues beyond the open door, but you make yourself wait.

You run your hands along the luggage racks. Dust. A single glove. A ticket stub punched so many times it is more hole than paper.

Beneath the conductor’s fold-down seat, wedged against the wall, is a leather notebook.

The first pages are a passenger list, written in a careful copperplate hand. Nearly every name has been crossed out. The ink of the oldest lines has faded to the colour of weak tea.

One entry near the end has not been crossed out:

<span class="ticket-text">Seat 13 — M.</span>

The last line on the page is your name.

$name.

When you touch it, the ink smears. It is still wet.

<span class="examine">(link: "Look under the seats")[(set: $hasLantern to true)(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">Your fingers close around a cold brass handle. A hooded railway lantern, still half full of paraffin. When you turn the wick, it gives a low, steady light. You keep it.</span>]</span>

The crying beyond the door stops, as if someone is listening.

{<div class="choices">[[Go toward the crying →->Carriage 2]]</div>}


:: Return to the Platform [flicker] {"position": "725,1700", "size": "100,100"}
(unless: $clues contains "station-sign")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "station-sign"))]You turn back toward the iron door you came through.

The handle is so cold it burns. You pull. It doesn’t move.

Through the small window in the door, you can see the platform. That should be impossible. The train has been moving for minutes.

The platform is empty now. The benches are gone. The lamps have rusted on their posts as though years have passed since you stood there.

A sign hangs from one chain:

<span class="sign">ASHGROVE</span>

Someone has painted a single word across it in white: CLOSED.

Beneath the last working lamp stands a figure, facing the tracks. Waiting for a train that has already left.

It lifts its head.

The lights in the carriage flicker, and when they return, the window shows only fog.

Behind you, the crying has become quieter. Closer.

{<div class="choices">[[Go toward the crying →->Carriage 2]]</div>}


:: Carriage 2 [flicker] {"position": "900,900", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 2)
The door closes behind you.

Carriage Two looks almost identical to the first. The same worn velvet seats, the same flickering brass lamps, and the same suffocating silence.

Except this carriage isn’t empty.

Halfway down the aisle, a woman sits alone beside the window. A tarnished brass number above her seat reads 13.

Her dark hair hangs loosely around her shoulders. She wears a pale blue dress, and her hands tremble as she clutches a small photograph.

You recognize the sound immediately.

She’s the woman you heard crying.

As you approach, she hurriedly wipes her eyes.

“Oh. I didn’t realize there was anyone else aboard.”

She forces a weak smile.

“Have you seen a little girl? About six years old? Brown hair, wearing a yellow coat?”

You shake your head.

Her expression falls.

“I see.”

She looks down at the photograph.

“Her name is…”

She pauses.

Her brow furrows.

“That’s strange.”

She turns the photograph over, searching for something written on the back.

“I can’t remember her name.”

The carriage lights flicker.

For a brief moment, you notice something peculiar.

The photograph she’s holding is completely blank.

When the lights stabilize, the image of a little girl has returned.

The woman looks up at you.

“Please. I think something is happening to me.”

What do you do?

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Sit beside her and offer to help")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 2))(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust + 1)(go-to: "Mara - Help")]
(link: "Ask why she believes her daughter is aboard")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 5))(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust - 1)(go-to: "Mara - Question")]
(link: "Examine the photograph more closely")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 8))(unless: $clues contains "mara-photo")[(set: $clues to $clues + (a: "mara-photo"))](go-to: "Mara - Photograph")]
(link: "Ignore the woman and continue down the aisle")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 3))(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust - 2)(go-to: "Mara - Ignore")]
</div>}


:: Mara - Help {"position": "1175,1075", "size": "100,100"}
You take the seat opposite her.

“Let’s start with what you remember.”

The woman exhales shakily. “My name is Mara. I remember leaving my house. It was raining, and I was supposed to pick up my daughter.”

She presses her fingers against her temples. “But I don’t remember getting to the station.”

You ask whether she remembers boarding the train.

“No.” She looks toward the window. “Actually, I don’t remember buying a ticket, either.”

Her voice drops to a whisper. “Do you?”

Your ticket is still in your pocket.

“Would you stay with me? Just until we find her?”

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->Mara's Decision]]</div>}


:: Mara - Question [flicker] {"position": "1325,1075", "size": "100,100"}
“Why do you think your daughter is on this train?”

Mara looks startled. “Because... she was with me.”

“At the station?”

“Yes. No. I...”

She stares down at the photograph. “I remember holding her hand.”

You ask what happened next.

“I remember letting go.”

The lights flicker. For an instant, a small hand appears pressed against the window beside her.

You blink. It’s gone.

“What?” Mara whispers. “What did you see?”

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->Mara's Decision]]</div>}


:: Mara - Photograph {"position": "1500,1075", "size": "100,100"}
“May I see that photograph?”

Mara hesitates, then hands it over.

A little girl in a yellow coat stands smiling in front of a house. Behind her, in an upstairs window, you notice a dark silhouette.

You tilt the photograph toward the light.

The silhouette is gone. Words have appeared across the glass:

//SHE NEVER BOARDED.//

You nearly drop the photograph.

“What’s wrong?” Mara asks.

You look again. The message has vanished.

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->Mara's Decision]]</div>}


:: Mara - Ignore [flicker] {"position": "1675,1075", "size": "100,100"}
You decide against getting involved. Whatever is happening aboard this train, you have enough problems of your own.

“Wait,” the woman calls. “Please. I don’t want to be alone.”

You reach the connecting door.

Then a child’s voice whispers, “Mommy?”

You turn. The woman is smiling at the empty seat beside her.

“There’s my girl.”

The lights flicker. When they return, the woman is crying again.

{<div class="choices">[[Continue →->Mara's Decision]]</div>}


:: Mara's Decision {"position": "1075,1375", "size": "100,100"}
The train suddenly lurches. A metallic screech echoes through the carriage.

Mara grips the edge of her seat. “What’s happening?”

The overhead speaker crackles.

<div class="speaker">“Attention, passengers. Please be advised that personal belongings, including memories, may be misplaced during transit. Management accepts no responsibility for items left behind.”</div>
The speaker clicks off.

“Memories?” Mara whispers.

She turns her photograph around. The little girl’s face has disappeared.

“Please,” she says, standing. “I don’t know what’s happening, but I can’t stay here. Will you help me?”

(if: $maraTrust >= 1)[Mara looks at you with a flicker of hope.

]\
(else-if: $maraTrust <= -2)[She keeps her distance, as though afraid you might walk away again.

]\
(else:)[She waits for an answer, searching your face.

]\
{<div class="choices">
(link: "Promise to help Mara find her daughter")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 3))(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust + 2)(set: $maraFollowing to true)(set: $passengers to $passengers + 1)(go-to: "Carriage 2 Exit")]
(link: "Let Mara accompany you, but make no promises")[(set: $maraFollowing to true)(set: $passengers to $passengers + 1)(go-to: "Carriage 2 Exit")]
(link: "Tell Mara to wait while you investigate")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 2))(set: $maraFollowing to false)(set: $maraWaiting to true)(go-to: "Carriage 2 Exit")]
(link: "Refuse to help and leave her behind")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 5))(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust - 2)(set: $maraFollowing to false)(go-to: "Carriage 2 Exit")]
</div>}


:: Carriage 2 Exit {"position": "800,1050", "size": "100,100"}
(if: $maraFollowing)[Mara walks a few paces behind you. She holds the photograph so tightly its corners bend.]
(else-if: $maraWaiting)[“I’ll be right here,” Mara says, sitting back down in Seat 13. She does not look as though she believes you.]
(else:)[You leave Mara in Seat 13. Her quiet sobbing follows you down the aisle.]

A brass plaque hangs above the connecting door.

**CARRIAGE III — DINING**

Beneath it, someone has scratched a warning into the wood:

//THE HUNGRY ARE NEVER SATISFIED.//

From beyond the door comes the scrape of silverware against porcelain.

Then laughter.

A child’s laughter.

{<div class="choices">[[Enter Carriage Three →->Carriage 3]]</div>}


:: Carriage 3 {"position": "800,1250", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 3)

The dining car smells of fresh bread and something faintly metallic. Every table is set for dinner, but no one is eating.

At the far end of the carriage, a boy sits alone, turning a silver pocket watch in his hands.

The second hand moves backward.

He looks up as you enter.

“You’re late,” he says.

(if: $maraFollowing)[Mara’s hand finds your sleeve. “That boy,” she whispers. “He’s dressed like someone from an old photograph.”

]\
{<div class="choices">
(link: "“Late for what?”")[(go-to: "Thomas")]
(link: "Sit down at one of the set tables")[(go-to: "The Feast")]
(link: "Read the place cards on the tables")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 8))(go-to: "Place Cards")]
</div>}


:: Thomas {"position": "900,1700", "size": "100,100"}
The boy snaps the watch shut.

“Late for dinner. Everyone’s late, on this train. Late, or early, or a little bit lost.” He says it the way a child repeats something he has heard an adult say too many times.

“My name is Thomas. I’ve been travelling on my own.” He sits up straighter, proud of it. “I’m nine.”

The watch ticks backward in his palm.

“I’m winding it back,” he explains. “If I wind it far enough, I’ll be at the station again, and this time I won’t get on.”

(if: $clues contains "newspaper")[You think of the newspaper in the first carriage. //A boy, nine years old, travelling alone.//

]\
<span class="examine">(link: "Sit with him and listen")[(unless: $clues contains "girl-on-platform")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "girl-on-platform"))](set: $hasWatch to true)(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">You sit. Thomas swings his legs, too short to reach the floor.

“There’s a girl who comes to the platform,” he says. “Every night. She wears a yellow coat. She waves at the train like she’s waiting for someone to wave back.” He frowns. “She was little when I first saw her. She’s grown up now. She still comes.”

(if: $maraFollowing)[Beside you, Mara has gone very still.

]\
He presses the watch into your hand. “You keep it. It doesn’t work backward fast enough for me. Maybe it’ll work forward for you.”

The second hand ticks against your palm, sharp as a pin.</span>]</span>

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Ask Thomas to come with you")[(set: $thomasFollowing to true)(set: $passengers to $passengers + 1)(go-to: "Dining Car")]
(link: "Leave him to his watch")[(go-to: "Dining Car")]
</div>}


:: The Feast {"position": "1075,1700", "size": "100,100"}
You pull out a chair. The moment you sit, a plate is in front of you that was not there before.

It is the meal you loved most as a child. Exactly as it was made for you, years ago, in a kitchen you have not stood in for a very long time. Steam rises from it. It smells like being safe.

(if: $sanity < 60)[Your hands are shaking. You are so tired, and it would be so easy.

]\
(else:)[Your stomach aches with a hunger you didn’t know you had.

]\
(if: $maraFollowing)[Mara does not sit. “Don’t,” she says quietly. “Look at the others.”

]\
At the next table, the cutlery is laid out for a guest who isn’t there. The napkin is folded around nothing. The scratched words above the door return to you. //The hungry are never satisfied.//

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Eat")[(set: $ateFeast to true)(set: $sanity to (min: 100, $sanity + 20))(if: $clues's length > 0)[(set: $forgotten to $clues's 1st)(set: $clues to $clues - (a: $forgotten))](go-to: "Dining Car")]
(link: "Push the plate away")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 4))(go-to: "Dining Car")]
</div>}


:: Place Cards {"position": "1250,1700", "size": "100,100"}
(unless: $clues contains "place-cards")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "place-cards"))]Every seat in the dining car is reserved.

Each place setting has a small cream card, written in the same careful copperplate as the conductor’s notebook. A name, and beneath it, a date.

//October 28, 1891.// //March 3, 1952.// //August 9, 1978.// The dates go on and on, table after table, none of them the same.

At the table nearest the door, the card reads //$name//.

Beneath your name is tonight’s date.

(if: $maraFollowing)[Mara picks up the card beside yours. Her name is on it. She sets it face down without reading the date, and you do not ask her to.

]\
At the head of the longest table there is a place set for the conductor. His card has no date at all.

<span class="examine">(link: "Lift the conductor’s napkin")[(set: $hasKeycard to true)(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">Folded inside is a stamped brass card on a short chain. <span class="sign">LOCOMOTIVE — CREW ONLY</span> You slip it into your pocket.</span>]</span>

{<div class="choices">[[Step back from the tables->Dining Car]]</div>}


:: Dining Car {"position": "1425,1700", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 3)
{(if: (history:)'s last is "The Feast" and $ateFeast)[
<p>You eat until the plate is empty. Warmth spreads through you. Your thoughts become clear and calm.</p>
(if: $forgotten is not "")[<p>Afterwards you try to remember something you saw earlier tonight. Something important. It is gone. There is only a clean, empty space where it used to be, like a pale square on wallpaper where a picture once hung.</p>]
(if: $maraFollowing)[<p>Mara watches you with an expression you can’t read.</p>]
]
(else-if: (history:)'s last is "The Feast")[
<p>You push the plate away. It is the hardest thing you have done tonight. The hunger stays with you, a dull ache under your ribs, but your head stays your own.</p>
]
(else-if: (history:)'s last is "Thomas" and $thomasFollowing)[
<p>Thomas hops down from his chair and takes his place behind you, as solemn as a soldier.</p>
]
(else-if: (history:)'s last is "Thomas")[
<p>Thomas has opened his watch again. He does not look up as you leave.</p>
]
(else-if: (history:)'s last is "Place Cards")[
<p>You put your card back exactly where you found it.</p>
]}

The dining car waits around you. Somewhere, silver scrapes against porcelain, though no one is eating.

