:: Carriage 3 Exit {"position": "200,1875", "size": "100,100"}
(if: $maraWaiting and not $maraFollowing and $maraTrust >= 0)[(set: $maraFollowing to true)(set: $maraWaiting to false)(set: $passengers to $passengers + 1)Footsteps hurry up behind you. It is Mara, out of breath, the photograph in her fist.

“I couldn’t sit there alone,” she says. “Not with the lights doing that. I’m coming with you.”

]A brass plaque hangs above the next door.

**CARRIAGE IV — SLEEPER**

Beneath it, scratched into the wood in the same hurried hand you saw on the armrest:

//DON’T FALL ASLEEP.//

(if: $thomasFollowing)[Thomas reads it aloud, then looks up at you. “That’s good advice,” he says. “I wish I’d had it.”

]\
Beyond the door, something is breathing. Many somethings, slow and even, all at once.

{<div class="choices">[[Enter Carriage Four →->Carriage 4]]</div>}


:: Carriage 4 {"position": "375,1875", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 4)(unless: $hasLantern)[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 8))]
(if: $hasLantern)[You raise the lantern. Its light slides along a narrow corridor lined with curtained berths, upper and lower, stretching farther than the carriage should allow.]
(else:)[It is dark. Truly dark. You feel your way forward with one hand on the wall. Curtains brush your face like cobwebs. Somewhere ahead is a faint grey glow, very far away.]

Behind every curtain, someone is sleeping. You can hear them. They breathe together, in and out, in time with the rocking of the train.

It is a soothing sound. That is the worst thing about it.

(if: $maraFollowing and $maraTrust < 0)[(set: $maraFollowing to false)(set: $maraSlept to true)(set: $passengers to $passengers - 1)Mara stops beside an empty lower berth. Its curtain is drawn back, the sheets turned down, waiting.

“I’ll just rest here,” she says. “You don’t need me.” She does not look at you. “You’ve made that clear enough.”

She lies down. The curtain falls shut by itself. Her breathing joins the others.]
(else-if: $maraFollowing)[Mara holds on to your arm. “Don’t let me stop walking,” she whispers.]

(if: $hasWatch)[In your pocket, the watch ticks backward, sharp and wrong. It keeps you awake.

]\
