(link: "Keep moving toward the far door")[(go-to: "The Voice")]
</div>}


:: Search the Berths {"position": "550,1875", "size": "100,100"}
(if: $hasLantern)[(unless: $clues contains "unsent-letter")[(set: $clues to it + (a: "unsent-letter"))]You move from berth to berth, lifting the curtains a few inches with the lantern held high. Faces turned to the wall. A hand hanging over the edge, fingers curled. None of them stir.

One berth is empty. On the mattress, a suitcase. Your suitcase. You would know it anywhere.

The luggage tag is in your handwriting. Under //Destination// you wrote one word: <span class="ticket-text">HOME</span>.

<span class="examine">(link: "Open the suitcase")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 4))(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">Inside there is nothing but a letter, sealed, addressed in your own hand. The stamp was never cancelled. The ink has run, as though it was carried through rain.

Through the thin paper you can make out a single line:

//I’m on the last train. Leave the porch light on.//</span>]</span>
](else:)[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 12))You feel along the curtains in the dark, searching for anything you can use.

Your hand closes on a wrist.

It is cold, and it holds on. For a long moment it will not let go. Then, slowly, the fingers loosen, and the arm slides back behind the curtain, and the breathing goes on as if nothing happened.

You find nothing else. You do not try again.]

The breathing grows louder. Slower. Your eyelids are heavy.

(if: $hasWatch)[The watch ticks backward against your palm, sharp as a pin, and you jerk awake. You are still standing.

]\
(else-if: $sanity >= 35)[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 6))You bite the inside of your cheek until you taste copper. You stay awake. Barely.

]\
(else:)[You are so tired. The nearest berth is open. The pillow is cool. One of the sleepers murmurs something that sounds like your name.

]\
