</div>}


:: Lost Property {"position": "725,1875", "size": "100,100"}
Mara has stopped at a wire rack near the middle of the carriage. A painted sign above it reads <span class="sign">LOST PROPERTY</span>.

Umbrellas. A single red mitten. Spectacles with one lens cracked. A wedding ring in a saucer.

Mara lifts down a black umbrella. It is still wet. A paper tag hangs from the handle:

<span class="ticket-text">FOUND AT ASHGROVE CROSSING</span>

“This is mine,” she says. Her voice is very calm. “I had it when I left the house. It was raining so hard. I was late to pick her up, and the crossing lights were flashing, and I thought…” She stops. “I thought I could make it.”

She turns to you.

“Did I ever pick her up?”

|talk>[{<div class="choices">
(if: $clues contains "mara-photo" or $clues contains "girl-on-platform")[(link: "Tell her what you saw: she never boarded")[(set: $maraKnows to true)(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust + 1)(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 3))(rerun: ?data)(replace: ?talk)[<p>You tell her about the words on the photograph. (if: $clues contains "girl-on-platform")[About the girl in the yellow coat who waves at the train, who has grown up.]</p><p>Mara listens without interrupting. When you finish, she is crying, but it is a different kind of crying from before.</p><p>“She never boarded,” Mara says. “Because I never got there. She waited, and someone else came for her.” She lets out a breath that is almost a laugh. “She grew up.”</p><p>She hangs the umbrella back on the rack. Her hand, when she takes yours, is warm for the first time.</p>(if: not ((history:) contains "Search the Berths"))[(link: "Search the berths")[(go-to: "Search the Berths")]](link: "Keep moving toward the far door")[(go-to: "The Voice")]]]]
(link: "Tell her a kind lie: her daughter is waiting at the next stop")[(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust + 1)(rerun: ?data)(replace: ?talk)[<p>“She’s waiting for you,” you say. “At the next stop. She’s fine.”</p><p>Mara searches your face for a long moment. Then she nods, and holds the wet umbrella to her chest like a child, and does not ask again.</p>(if: not ((history:) contains "Search the Berths"))[(link: "Search the berths")[(go-to: "Search the Berths")]](link: "Keep moving toward the far door")[(go-to: "The Voice")]]]
(link: "Say nothing")[(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust - 1)(rerun: ?data)(replace: ?talk)[<p>You say nothing. The silence answers for you.</p><p>Mara looks away first. “I see,” she says, the same way she said it when you first met.</p>(if: not ((history:) contains "Search the Berths"))[(link: "Search the berths")[(go-to: "Search the Berths")]](link: "Keep moving toward the far door")[(go-to: "The Voice")]]]
</div>}]


:: The Voice [flicker] {"position": "900,1875", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 4)The far door opens onto the gangway between carriages. Here the train is open to the night. Cold air. Iron plates shifting underfoot. Fog pours past on both sides like a river.

The wheels go quiet.

And someone, out in the fog, calls your name.

<div class="voice-call">“$name.”</div>
It is a voice you know. You can’t remember from where, but you know it, the way you know your own front door. It sounds worried. It sounds like it has been calling for a long time.

<div class="voice-call">“$name, come home.”</div>
(if: $clues contains "warning")[//If you hear someone calling your name from outside the train, do not answer.//]

(if: $maraFollowing)[Mara has gone rigid beside you. Out in the fog, a smaller voice is calling too. //Mommy? Mommy, where are you?// Mara takes a step toward the railing.

]\
(if: $thomasFollowing)[Thomas has his hands pressed over his ears. His eyes are shut tight.

]\
<div class="voice-timer" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
<span class="examine">(link: "Lean over the railing and look for who is calling")[(set: $sanity to (max: 0, $sanity - 25))(rerun: ?data)<span class="examined">You lean out into the cold. Far below, where the tracks should be, there is only fog, and in the fog a figure stands with a lamp, looking up at the train. You cannot see its face. It raises the lamp, and for a moment you are sure it is wearing your coat.</span>]</span>

{<div class="choices">
(link: "Answer the voice")[(set: $answeredVoice to true)(go-to: "Nowhere Station")]
(if: $maraFollowing)[(link: "Take Mara’s hand and hold on")[(set: $heldMara to true)(set: $maraTrust to $maraTrust + 1)(go-to: "The Silence")]]
(link: "Say nothing")[(go-to: "The Silence")]
</div>}
(after: 20s)[(go-to: "The Silence")]


:: The Silence {"position": "1075,1875", "size": "100,100"}
You do not answer.

The voice calls once more, fainter. Then the wheels find their rhythm again, and the fog closes, and there is nothing out there but the night.

(if: $heldMara)[Mara’s fingers are locked around yours so tightly it hurts. She does not let go until the voices have faded completely. “Thank you,” she breathes. “I would have gone. I would have gone to her.”]
(else-if: $maraFollowing and $maraTrust < 2)[(set: $maraFollowing to false)(set: $maraLost to true)(set: $passengers to $passengers - 1)You hear the gate in the railing creak.

When you turn, Mara is gone. On the iron plates where she stood, the photograph lies face down. The fog has already swallowed her. Somewhere out in it, a woman is calling a child’s name. You realise you never learned it.]
(else-if: $maraFollowing)[Mara has her eyes closed and her lips pressed together. She does not answer the small voice. When it stops, she lets out a long, shaking breath. “I couldn’t,” she says. “I trusted you were right.”]

(if: $thomasFollowing)[Thomas lowers his hands. “Is it over?” he asks. You tell him it is.

]\
Ahead, at the end of the gangway, a heavy door is set into the front of the train. It is warm to the touch. Behind it, something roars.

{<div class="choices">[[Approach the engine door →->The Engine Door]]</div>}


:: The Engine Door {"position": "1250,1875", "size": "100,100"}
(set: $carriage to 5)A brass plate is riveted to the door:

<span class="sign">LOCOMOTIVE — CREW ONLY</span>

Heat radiates through the iron. You can hear the fire behind it, and the clank of a shovel, steady as a heartbeat.

(if: $hasKeycard)[Beneath the handle is a narrow brass slot, exactly the width of the card in your pocket.

]\
(if: $trustsConductor)[You think of the conductor’s tired eyes. He told you the truth, as far as you can tell. Perhaps he would open the door if you asked.

]\
{<div class="choices">
(if: $hasKeycard)[(link: "Slide the brass card into the slot")[(go-to: "The Locomotive")]]
(if: $trustsConductor)[(link: "Knock, and ask the conductor to let you in")[(go-to: "The Locomotive")]]
